  "caption": "Quinn joined a Sunday footy team, pushed off hard on artificial turf, and the big toe bent way back. A teammate said to tape it and play on.\n\nTurf toe is a sprain under the big toe joint, usually from forced upward bending at push-off. Playing through it can make it linger much longer.\n\nWhat can help: tape early on to limit upward bending (to protect it, not to play through pain), a stiff-soled shoe or stiff insert, keeping fit with cycling or swimming, and rebuilding calf and toe strength gradually. Return to sport once push-off feels pain-free.\n\nGet it checked if there's big swelling or bruising, you can't bear weight, or the toe feels unstable.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
